<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Telebras upped.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telebras upped.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings analysts Pat Jurczak and Vera Rossi have raised their rating for Brazilian telephone holding Telebras SA to buy from hold.</p>
<p>-- They said in a July 15 report that they made the upgrade based on price weakness. The company's stock price has fallen 17.5 percent since ING Barings cut its rating to hold July 10.</p>
<p>-- ING Barings cut its 12-month price target to $180 per American Depositary Receipt (ADR) from $187.50 because of reduced 1998 earnings estimates.</p>
<p>-- The analysts also reduced their five-year earnings growth rate to 20 percent from 22.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Telebras ADRs closed Tuesday at 134-10/16.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
